# Contributing to mau-coffee

Thank you for considering contributing! This file gives a quick, practical guide to reporting issues and submitting changes.

## Ways to contribute
- Report bugs or suggest features via Issues or email (bug@mau.coffee).
- Open a Pull Request (PR) for code, docs, or other improvements.
- Fix typos or improve documentation directly via PRs. :)

## Reporting issues
- Provide a short summary and steps to reproduce. Don't overthink it, just share what you see.
- Include expected vs actual behavior and relevant screenshots or logs, if possible.

## Pull request guidelines
- Fork the repo and create a feature branch: `git checkout -b my-change`. (Like usual)
- Keep PRs small and focused. Reference the related issue if available.
- Describe what you changed and why in the PR description. (Helps me understand or learn from your change!)

## Coding style
- Keep changes simple and consistent with existing PHP and file structure.
- Follow existing indentation and naming conventions. (No need to be perfect, just try to match the style.)

## Testing
- Verify locally by running the site in `docker-compose` and checking affected pages.
- If you change CSS, run `npm run build:css` or `npm run watch:css` during development. Try as much as possible to do it via tailwindcss.

## Commit messages
- Use short, descriptive commit messages (imperative tense). Also don't worry here, your contribution is more important, especially on side projects like that.

## Licensing
By contributing you agree that your contributions will be licensed under the project's MIT License (see `LICENCE`). Don't forget to include yourself in the copyright notice if you want to be credited. :)